{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1090404-humanity-check-input-apreciated","id":1090404,"title":"Humanity check? Input apreciated","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-09T11:55:42-07:00","id":1090404,"title":"Humanity check? Input apreciated","content":"The story (background is important I think): The player M is a humanity 8 vampire (60+ human years, 25 vampire ones) sympathetic and likable guy. He has a friend L (also player character, humanity 5 these days) since human days and they have simultaneously been sired as Vampire. They have spent a lot of time together, despite changing views, generally considered good friends. A Human that had a favor to collect from M reached out to him to ask him to set up a meeting between L and the human. M obliged and setup this meeting at which point the Human asked L to make him a Vampire. L lied to the human saying he would do it, took him outside of town and killed him. The human has risen as a ghost entity capable of possessing L and having him walk into the sunlight (shortly, 3 lethal dmg), the Anchor of this entity has come into the hands of M and after talking to it and learning of the what L has done he has decided to give it back to L. M is aware of the dangers this poses to L.<br /> <br /> the question: Does this invoke a humanity check for player M and if so at which rank?<br /> <br /> I am ST-ing the game and am inclined to waive the humanity check here, because of the circumstances. M has offered to help L find another solution for the vampire request and didn't condone the murder or knew of it beforehand. Also there is no way for M to stop the ghost entity from pursuing his goal<br /> <br /> Anyways, different viewpoints and opinions appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7177-kurt","name":"Kurt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7177_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T12:33:40-07:00","id":1090433,"title":"","content":"Which edition is this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T12:50:49-07:00","id":1090441,"title":"","content":"A Humanity check for M? For what specifically? Giving L a tool to prevent a ghost from maiming or killing L?<br /> He had no part or knowledge of the murder so no check regarding that unless he had reason to suspect the nature of the human's request. Because if he did, he facilitated a murder.<br /> If I was STing, I wouldn't do a Humanity check for M unless he willfully refuses to put the ghost to rest or if, in assisting in that task it entails harming someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T13:11:40-07:00","id":1090450,"title":"","content":"edition is B&amp;S with a bit of homebrew on the ghost.<br /> <br /> a humanity check for M for giving L the item that anchors the ghost, thus placing the ghost in his vicinity knowing of the ghosts intentions.<br /> to M's knowledge there is no way to put the ghost to rest other than fulfilling it's purpose (that being killing L)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7177-kurt","name":"Kurt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7177_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T13:28:23-07:00","id":1090457,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind, Humanity Detatchment in 2nd Edition (B&amp;S) is about losing touch with the human experience, not about adherence to a behavioral code. Breaking Points are triggered not by sins, but by experiences that force the character to face their inhumanity - &quot;why don't I feel remorse for killing this person?&quot; or &quot;how did I survive that?&quot; or &quot;it's been so long since I talked to a human, I forgot how sensitive they can be.&quot; etc. I don't really see anything about M putting the ghost in L's vicinity would cause M to lose his grip on what it means to be human, so I don't see any need for a Detachment roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-09-2017, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T15:51:03-07:00","id":1090506,"title":"","content":"I agree with all of the other posts above, I wouldn't do a humanity check unless he has the knowledge it would do the ghost harm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T04:23:14-07:00","id":1090675,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the responses, I will stick to no check required then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7177-kurt","name":"Kurt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7177_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T05:43:55-07:00","id":1091083,"title":"","content":"I might be tempted to call for a Humanity check on the basis that this is a friend from their mortal days (despite being a Vampire now) who they plan to give an Anchor, knowingly risking their friend's life with the intention of helping a ghost move on (decidedly supernatural). On top of that, the ghost's reasons for wanting to gain vengeance against L is that they wanted to be sired by L, but got tricked and killed instead.<br /> <br /> Edit: basically, betraying someone from your mortal days for reasons steeped deeply in their new (un)life, coming fully to terms with the fact your friend is a Vampire -- and by extension that you're a Vampire, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 05-11-2017, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T23:28:39-07:00","id":1091440,"title":"","content":"I can follow your reasoning, at which level breaking point would you class that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7177-kurt","name":"Kurt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7177_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T02:37:24-07:00","id":1091467,"title":"","content":"Without knowing what happened to L, there would be no way to determine what level a breaking point this situation would be. I assume everyone here is human. I like to imagine how out of character the act is to me, as a human I feel I'm something of an expert on Humanity. Potentially setting up a friend of at least 25 years to be killed even though they didn't actually do anything to me sounds like something I would never do, but maybe I'm not very judgmental.<br /> <br /> If L dies it would be 2, unless M didn't think L would end up dead then it would be 4. Injury could be 5, 6, or 7 depending on the severity and no injury maybe puts it at 8. M's behavior sounds antisocial to me. That balances against the impersonal nature of whatever the ghost does to L. I would wait to see what happens to L then do a humanity check. If nothing else, M did unintentionally help someone become ghosted. I would sum up the entire scenario into one check. The downside to Humanity 8 is lots of things are breaking points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T02:19:53-07:00","id":1091875,"title":"","content":"Nothing has happened to L yet, nest session is Thursday.<br /> Also it's not like L didn't do anything, he did kill the human that lead to the creation of the Ghost after M requested him not to kill him and that he had other options to help out the human.<br /> (Just re-read that sentence and you said 'didn't do anything to me' this is correct, but how would you act when your friend of 25 years kills someone you introduced to him after your express request not to do so?)<br /> <br /> From M's perspective he is returning the anchor to L distancing himself from the situation making it like it was before he got involved (L provided the anchor to M for research) but now of course M is aware of the risks that poses to L. his reasoning is basically 'I tried to help you before you got into this mess, you got into this situation by not listening to my advice or reaching out to me to find another solution, so now you get to be in, and solve, this problem by yourself.'<br /> <br /> I could 'postpone' any humanity check to the moment where something actually has happened to L and M finds out what that was.<br /> <br /> Assuming IC motivation and reasoning might make a difference, M did research a way for the Ghost to peacefully transcend to the afterlife but found that only to be possible when the Ghosts purpose has been fulfilled and although there are ways to temporarily banish the Ghost the Ghost would eventually come back to haunt L (so banishing the Ghost would only extend the suffering of that entity)<br /> <br /> I like all the feedback I get, thank you all again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7177-kurt","name":"Kurt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7177_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T15:37:41-07:00","id":1092120,"title":"","content":"I would no longer associate with the killer, but I wouldn't try to get them killed. Anyway, sounds like L's death would be more accidental (4). I think you should postpone as you say. The important factors to me would be how M responds to finding out what happens to L. I think the human response would be regretful and conflicted. Since L is a player character, I assume he isn't likely to die, so as long as that holds true, I might skip the roll unless the player wants to take the chance and simply give the beat for a proper human (in character) response to this mess. M should feel sympathy for victims of violence, even when the victim is an asshole. To me, that is the place for a humanity check, after M sees how the scenario plays out. How does M feel about what happens to the ghost and L? That would be the breaking point. I'm guessing they don't sing Kumbaya and the ghost walks into the light. I sense tragedy is on the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T19:27:28-07:00","id":1092626,"title":"","content":"theirs a story in the strix anthology... &quot;Lullay, Lullay&quot; it mentioned a child looking vampire going through her efforts to &quot;Mend the sheeps clothing&quot;<br /> <br /> one of the things her and her ghould did, was take a marker and measure her height, over and over at the same exact point...<br /> <br /> in 2nd edition, I thought, shouldnt that be a breaking point at 8 or so, maybe I'm over complicating it, unlikely a vamp with a Strix actively after her has humanity that high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}